RenHDrum 0.3.0, built from the upstream v0.3.0 source tree
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/tree/v0.3.0

The release binary at
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/releases/download/v0.3.0/renhdrum-v0.3.0.zip
(assets: renhdrum-v030.dll, renhdrum-v030.h, SHA256SUMS-v030.txt) imports
VCRUNTIME140.dll, which this project does not ship: on a machine without the
Visual C++ redistributable the haptics would silently fall back to the standard
rumble. renhdrum.dll here is therefore rebuilt from that same source with the C
runtime linked statically, so it depends on the system DLLs only.

Build, from a checkout of the v0.3.0 tag:

    set RUSTFLAGS=-C target-feature=+crt-static
    cargo build --release

The result was 414208 bytes with these dependencies:

    api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll
    KERNEL32.dll
    ntdll.dll

No VCRUNTIME140.dll, no MSVCP140.dll, no api-ms-win-crt-*.dll. The export table
is identical to the upstream DLL (47 names, compared with dumpbin /exports), so
the C ABI and the renhdrum_version() check are unchanged: 0x000300.

renhdrum.h is the upstream v0.3.0 header, byte for byte.

5b4821a9695ca01c1c91f3b3f52f25c97d2b8894e8206c6071caf52b26bad655  renhdrum.dll
ea23a7843ec471799adab6e1af1c85406aed505af2d8b57df03d7cb48ecac358  renhdrum.h

For reference, the upstream release binary was 299008 bytes with sha256
33c88b343fa49627cc09fcd0cee7e46f5a85e16e77f1d404e44574d42eaa74e8; it is not
shipped here.

LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and NOTICE are copied from the same source tree: the
core of RenHDrum is dual licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, and NOTICE asks for
"Copyright (c) 2026 Three-Dola" to be kept. The GPL-3.0-or-later parts of that
project (integrations/brontide, integrations/recomp-c/reference) are not used
here: the host calls the prebuilt library through its C ABI and does not build
any of its sources.
